WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.720
"Black Widow" may feel like a step backwards
for the timeline of the Marvel Cinematic Universe,

00:00:05.720 --> 00:00:09.850
but the ending to the story says a lot about
what's next for the MCU.

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:14.760
From Natasha's fate to the future of Yelena,
this is the ending of "Black Widow," explained.

00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:20.519
Examining Natasha Romanoff's ending in "Black
Widow" is impossible without taking the nature

00:00:20.519 --> 00:00:23.220
of the film as a prequel into account.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.630
After all, we know where she's eventually
headed.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:28.980
The ending of "Black Widow" just helps to
set it all up.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.190
By the end of the film, she's got the blonde
hair we first see her sporting in "Avengers:

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:38.570
Infinity War," and one movie later, she sacrifices
herself to save her friends in "Avengers:

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.570
Endgame."

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:44.670
The movie also elaborates on Natasha's involvement
in Cap's team of secret Avengers that operated

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.350
covertly in the aftermath of "Civil War."

00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:51.960
It turns out that she's the one responsible
for picking up the Quinjet that allows Team

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.530
Cap to continue running secret missions across
the globe for the next two years.

00:00:56.530 --> 00:01:01.050
When "Black Widow" begins, Natasha declares
herself out of the game, but by the end of

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:05.960
it, she's got a new sense of purpose, making
her the driving force behind the secret Avengers

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.720
team that heads out to help the world in ways
the MCU still hasn't fully shown us.

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:16.159
We don't really know exactly how she went
about assembling Sam, Steve, and Wanda to

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:20.369
go out and help people once again, but now
we know she was an integral part of forming

00:01:20.369 --> 00:01:23.189
the group and not just following her friends
into battle.

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:28.560
If Natasha's journey in "Black Widow" is about
reconnecting to her sense of purpose after

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:33.490
losing some of her hope during "Captain America:
Civil War," her sister Yelena's journey is

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:37.649
about discovering that she can actually have
a sense of purpose to call her own.

00:01:37.649 --> 00:01:42.310
For years, Yelena has served the Red Room
and only the Red Room, and when her newfound

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:47.360
freedom comes, it merges with all of that
cold resolve she developed as a trained killer,

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:49.890
turning her into a determined force of nature.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:54.950
This, of course, naturally sets her up to
be the next Black Widow in the MCU, but her

00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:00.479
path is complicated by the arrival of Contessa
Valentina Allegra de Fontaine in her life

00:02:00.479 --> 00:02:04.740
at some point after the events of the film,
as seen in the movie's post-credits scene

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.469
with her and Val meeting over Natasha's grave.

00:02:07.469 --> 00:02:09.090
"Don't call me that."

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.090
"Copy."

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:15.069
Thanks to Valentina's influence, Yelena has
found steady work as a hired gun once again,

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:17.360
but whose side is she really on?

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.540
Does she even know?

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:22.849
Is Valentina's knack for manipulation and
temptation simply another form of control

00:02:22.849 --> 00:02:25.569
that Yelena can feel but not see?

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:29.670
However it all shakes out, Yelena came out
of "Black Widow" with a new sense of freedom

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:34.260
and determination, and the moment she discovers
someone is trying to pull her strings, they'd

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.890
better run in the other direction.

00:02:37.090 --> 00:02:41.450
Natasha and Yelena's "mother," Melina Vostokoff,
is one of the more fascinating members of

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:46.409
the "Black Widow" cast because she seems to
jump between two worlds ﻿quite comfortably,

00:02:46.409 --> 00:02:47.599
even for a spy.

00:02:47.599 --> 00:02:52.680
On the one hand, she's been serving the Red
Room in an advanced capacity for a long time,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:57.849
working directly on the subjugation tactics
that helped her boss, Dreykov, retain an iron

00:02:57.849 --> 00:02:59.860
grip on the Widows for years.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.219
She seems to have no qualms at all about this,
even relishing the technology she's helped

00:03:04.219 --> 00:03:08.689
develop, right up until she realizes what
a dramatic impact it's had on the people she

00:03:08.689 --> 00:03:09.909
cares about.

00:03:09.909 --> 00:03:14.209
From there, she's eager to help bring Dreykov
down, and by the end of the film, she's apparently

00:03:14.209 --> 00:03:18.799
found a new place for herself as a kind of
caretaker to a group of orphaned Widows.

00:03:18.799 --> 00:03:23.730
We don't know yet what Melina does after she
and Alexei Shostakov fly off with the Widows

00:03:23.730 --> 00:03:24.730
in tow.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.510
Perhaps she just returns to her farm, helps
out when she can, and keeps tending to her

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:29.640
pigs.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:33.790
Perhaps she digs deeper into the worldwide
espionage community and helps Yelena to free

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:35.310
more Widows.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.790
Perhaps she just enjoys a quiet retirement.

00:03:37.790 --> 00:03:42.849
But as long as she's alive, Melina represents
an important figure in the MCU underworld,

00:03:42.849 --> 00:03:47.189
who at any moment could shift the balance
of power with what she knows and what she

00:03:47.189 --> 00:03:48.629
can do with that knowledge.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:54.980
Of the four "family" members that served undercover
in America during the "Black Widow" prologue,

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.799
Alexei Shostakov might be the most diminished
when we meet him again in the present day.

00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:04.069
While everyone else has had an undoubtedly
hard time, at least they weren't left to rot

00:04:04.069 --> 00:04:05.410
away in prison.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:08.939
And when we eventually catch up with him,
Alexei's glory days as the Red Guardian are

00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:13.920
clearly long gone, but over the course of
the film, he comes to find that he might still

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:17.269
have some power left in his worn-down super
soldier body.

00:04:17.269 --> 00:04:22.370
By the end of the movie, Alexei has limped
away into the sunset alongside Melina, and

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:24.970
where he goes from there, we don't really
know.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:28.990
He could choose retirement, but something
about his personality and his love of adventure

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:34.150
suggests that a longing for his glory days
would eventually lure him back out into the

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.150
world.

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:39.301
What that means for the larger superhero community
is anybody's guess, but going forward, it's

00:04:39.301 --> 00:04:43.270
important to remember that there's another
super soldier out there in the MCU.

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:47.949
With a super-powered U.S. Agent out in the
world — not to mention a new Captain America

00:04:47.949 --> 00:04:51.639
— Red Guardian might want to make his presence
known once again.

00:04:52.639 --> 00:04:56.840
Shortly before his death, Dreykov reveals
to Natasha that while his Red Room headquarters

00:04:56.840 --> 00:05:01.830
might be the hub of his operation, it doesn't
begin to convey the full scope of his power.

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:06.210
He's got what appears to be hundreds of Widow
operatives around the world, all under his

00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:10.190
direct control, ready to sway world governments
at a moment's notice.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:11.190
"They're manipulated.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.280
Fully conscious, but no choices."

00:05:13.280 --> 00:05:18.449
Fortunately, before the Red Room is destroyed,
Natasha manages to copy all of Dreykov's data,

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:23.370
giving her the locations of all of these Widows
and, perhaps, the opportunity for Yelena and

00:05:23.370 --> 00:05:25.770
her to free all of them in time.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:30.720
The key question, though, is what each of
these women might do if and when they're freed.

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:34.520
How many of them actually like what they're
doing and are perhaps predisposed to more

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:36.020
villainous tendencies?

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:40.550
How many of them will simply become adrift
and lost when their purpose is taken away?

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:45.180
How many will want to perhaps become future
Avengers or maybe SWORD agents?

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:49.740
There are a lot of lingering questions -- and
a lot of potential wild cards -- in that data

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:50.740
file.

00:05:51.740 --> 00:05:55.610
Perhaps no other figure in "Black Widow" better
exemplifies Dreykov's legacy of cruelty better

00:05:55.610 --> 00:06:01.270
than his own daughter, who spends most of
the film as the masked figure known as Taskmaster.

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:05.690
For years, Natasha has believed that she ordered
the killing of Dreykov's daughter, part of

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:09.830
the "red" in her ledger that she was going
to spend her life wiping clean.

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:14.889
But Dreykov actually managed to save the girl
... only to then transform her into a killing

00:06:14.889 --> 00:06:18.160
machine deployed against his most high-value
targets.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.330
By the end of the film, Dreykov's daughter
is freed by Natasha and Yelena, but it's still

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:27.229
an open question whether she can ever have
anything even resembling a normal life.

00:06:27.229 --> 00:06:31.440
Even more than the other Red Room Widows,
she exemplifies the depths of her father's

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:33.569
cruelty and ruthlessness.

00:06:33.569 --> 00:06:38.039
That leaves deep psychological scars along
with all the combat skills, and she might

00:06:38.039 --> 00:06:39.610
never fully heal.

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:43.479
But if she does feel like stepping back out
into the field, having Taskmaster fighting

00:06:43.479 --> 00:06:46.050
alongside the good guys would be a sight to
see.

00:06:47.050 --> 00:06:51.770
A key point of the "Black Widow" plot is Natasha's
realization that Dreykov -- the man she thought

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:56.610
she'd killed as part of her defection mission
to SHIELD -- is not only still alive but still

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:59.180
running the Red Room from a secret sky base.

00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:02.539
In fact, his grip on power is tighter than
it's ever been.

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:07.169
Sure, by the end of the film, Natasha has
managed to truly end Dreykov once and for

00:07:07.169 --> 00:07:11.629
all, but the character's legacy and its ripple
effects could be part of the MCU for years

00:07:11.629 --> 00:07:12.949
to come.

00:07:12.949 --> 00:07:17.270
Dreykov wasn't just a charismatic, powerful
leader with a firm grasp on what it took to

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:18.800
rule from the Red Room.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:23.129
He was also the keeper of a dangerous chemical
compound that allowed him to control even

00:07:23.129 --> 00:07:29.069
those closest to him in perpetuity, a technology
he stole from an American lab in 1995 and

00:07:29.069 --> 00:07:30.190
perfected.

00:07:30.190 --> 00:07:34.800
We know from the film that Dreykov wasn't
the first to experiment with chemical brainwashing,

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.220
and we also know that someone else developed
a formula to stop his mind-control tech in

00:07:39.220 --> 00:07:40.220
its tracks.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.759
So, what happens now?

00:07:41.759 --> 00:07:46.870
It's unlikely that Dreykov simply died with
no loose ends left in that technological chain.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:51.159
His legacy of pain and control doesn't end
with him, and we've perhaps only begun to

00:07:51.159 --> 00:07:54.280
see the implications of it in the wider MCU.

00:07:54.280 --> 00:07:58.510
Who knows where that mind-controlling chemical
might show up next and in what form?

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:03.490
The post-credits scene of "Black Widow" reveals
that Yelena has taken a job with Valentina

00:08:03.490 --> 00:08:08.669
Allegra de Fontaine -- an influential woman
who wields a still-mysterious amount of power

00:08:08.669 --> 00:08:13.319
in the Marvel espionage world -- and that
Val is preparing to send Yelena off to target

00:08:13.319 --> 00:08:14.590
Clint Barton.

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:18.940
Val tells Yelena that Clint is responsible
for Natasha's death during "Endgame," which

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:22.610
is a stretch, but if there's one thing we
learned about Val from "The Falcon and the

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:26.650
Winter Soldier," it's that she's not afraid
to play fast and loose with the truth to get

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:27.939
what she wants.

00:08:27.939 --> 00:08:31.979
This one scene creates major ties between
"Black Widow," "The Falcon and the Winter

00:08:31.979 --> 00:08:36.380
Soldier," and the upcoming "Hawkeye" series
that will star Clint and his young protege,

00:08:36.380 --> 00:08:37.479
Kate Bishop.

00:08:37.479 --> 00:08:41.029
We also know that Yelena will be making an
appearance, although we're not sure if she'll

00:08:41.029 --> 00:08:46.190
get to meet up with characters like John Walker,
aka Val's other major asset at the moment,

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:49.150
or the Power Broker Sharon Carter in the near
future.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:53.310
What we do know, though, is that Yelena's
willingness to go deeper into Marvel's world

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:58.260
of espionage means that she's primed to be
every bit the Black Widow her sister was ... and

00:08:58.260 --> 00:08:59.390
perhaps even more.

00:09:00.420 --> 00:09:04.740
Much has been made of Natasha Romanoff's declaration
in "Avengers: Endgame" that she had nothing

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:09.820
until she found her Avengers "family," particularly
in light of "Black Widow" and its status as

00:09:09.820 --> 00:09:12.750
a prequel to both "Infinity War" and "Endgame."

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:16.920
The film's trailers seemed to set up that
Natasha actually did have a family in some

00:09:16.920 --> 00:09:22.110
form all along, so why would she simply discount
them in favor of her new superhero pals?

00:09:22.110 --> 00:09:23.110
"Family Reunion,"

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:24.190
"You don't know everything about me.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:26.029
The Avengers weren't my first family."

00:09:26.029 --> 00:09:30.620
In the end, "Black Widow" does a very good
job explaining why Natasha felt that way and

00:09:30.620 --> 00:09:34.870
why she phrased that much-discussed "Endgame"
sentence the way she did.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:39.720
As the movie reveals, Natasha did have what
felt like a real family as a young girl, only

00:09:39.720 --> 00:09:42.820
to have it taken away from her in devastating
fashion.

00:09:42.820 --> 00:09:47.670
The trauma of that origin story ultimately
drove her to defect, join SHIELD, and become

00:09:47.670 --> 00:09:48.670
an Avenger.

00:09:48.670 --> 00:09:52.820
She found a sense of family with the Avengers,
and if she hadn't earned that through them,

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:56.800
she might never have been able to reconnect
with her original family the way she did.

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:01.810
So, by the end of the film, Natasha notes
that she actually had two families all along,

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:05.640
but it took finding the second one to open
her heart enough for her to rediscover the

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:06.640
first.

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:07.870
It's not a contradiction.

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:12.440
It's just a convoluted journey that still
allowed her to reach the same conclusion.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:16.360
Becoming an Avenger made her a better person,
and the ripple effects of doing good brought

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:19.980
her back to something she thought she'd lost
long ago.

